  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Start was the first initiative of UNCDF specifically targeting youth (aged 12-24). The Programme has supported 10 financial institutions in 8 African countries, such as Burkina Faso, DR Congo, Ethiopia, and Malawi. Under the new Digital@UNCDF strategy, UNCDF is now channeling its experience to support the development and scaling up of digital innovations that empower young people and smoothen their transition to adulthood, with the specific objective of increasing the number of youths engaged in entrepreneurship, decent employment, school, or further education and training.</narrative>
